# SOUNDNESS (P0): the completion proof walks a loop over a small literal
# List once per element (EvalListloop) and stops at the first element whose
# body cannot complete normally, declaring the whole loop `never` -- but a
# body that ends in `break` or `continue` also "cannot complete normally"
# while the loop itself then does. Everything after the loop is treated as
# dead and never checked: the list::at below compiles with no handler and
# no errors clause, then raises an undeclared IndexNotFound at run time.
loop x in [1, 2]:
    if x > 1:
        break
    x

list::at([1], 5)
